Z||000014||LarryB||09-21-2001||09:11 PM||||The origins of the 3.8 have been discussed here before so I won't go into the details (you can find them in the archives) other than to mention it predates the 305 by about 9 years, and the 3.8's predecessor goes back yet another 6 years.<P>When GM bought the design back from AMC in the mid-1970's it made some changes to make it easier to build the 3.8 on the same manufacturing lines as the 350.  <P>The 305 shares the same 3.48" stroke of the 350 (and the 262/4.3L) but it has a 3.736" bore vs the 4.3L & 350's 4.00". The 3.8 has a 3.400" stroke and 3.800" bore.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>The 4.3 is actually just a 350 with two cylinders lopped off.  It's predecessor is a 3.8, which I believe is a similar child of the 305</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
